1. Open Camunda Modeler or a bpmn-js demo app.
2. Drag two Pool elements (Participants) onto the canvas.
3. Use the Message Flow tool to connect from the body of Pool A to the body of Pool B. (This should work as expected.)
4. Select Pool B, and add a new Lane to it (right-click or use the context menu).
5. Immediately remove the newly added Lane from Pool B, so Pool B is back to a single lane.
6. Try to use the Message Flow tool again to connect from the body of Pool A to the body of Pool B.
   - Observe: You can only connect to the header of Pool B, not to its body (lane area).

